{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"78412f86-bd00-4aac-bef5-95c86bc41a2f","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Relevant stories were queried from the `worklore` MCP server (`suggest_for_project`), identifying the story `2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts`.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Fixed the Generator ([`gen.py`](file:///private/tmp/h-VRdYAW/gen.py#L10-L14))**:\n   - Changed the lower bound key in [`hr_target`](file:///private/tmp/h-VRdYAW/gen.py#L10-L14) from `\"value\"` to `\"start\"`:\n     ```python\n     def hr_target(step):\n         \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\"\"\"\n         lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n         return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}\n     ```\n2. **Documented in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///private/tmp/h-VRdYAW/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Detailed what was changed and why: `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\", \"end\"}` triggers Intervals.icu's Lap-HR / zone-mapped export mode (which snaps targets to Garmin's local watch zones), whereas `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\", \"end\"}` specifies an Instant-HR corridor export where exact calculated bpm values are exported directly to the watch.\n","duration_seconds":50.769336,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":214209,"output_tokens":1651,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":215860}}}
